# Path-scoped exclusions for the git-span PreToolUse advisor's uncovered-writes
# check. See packages/agent-hooks/src/common/advisor-ignore.ts for the grammar.

# .wiki/wiki/** is the wiki tool's auto-generated anchor mesh (rk64 hashes
# mirroring wiki-cited line ranges for staleness detection), not source the
# advisor should ask for a git span — a commit that only re-anchors a drifted
# wiki mesh file is not an uncovered implicit dependency.
.wiki/

# The plugin hook bundles are esbuild output from packages/agent-hooks/src,
# regenerated wholesale by `yarn build` and committed only so the plugins are
# installable. Every file under these two directories is generated, including
# each hooks.json.
#
# They are excluded because a checklist naming them is unactionable, not merely
# noisy: the skill these very bundles ship tells the agent "don't span
# generated/build output — span its inputs instead"
# (plugins-claude/git-span/skills/git-span/SKILL.md), so an agent held on a
# pure bundle-regeneration commit had no compliant move available. Every entry
# was a file it was forbidden to span, and the only exit was the bare retry the
# one-shot hold permits — which teaches dismissing the advisor outright. That is
# the opposite of what this list is for.
#
# The classifier cannot reach these on its own by design: it only classifies
# manifest-shaped paths, so a regenerated bundle is never suppressed by content.
# Declaring them here is the intended mechanism rather than a workaround —
# advisor-ignore.ts describes this file as the place a repo owner lists
# "generated output, vendored code, anything that will never get a span."
#
# Both patterns name the whole `hooks/` directory, deliberately at the same
# depth. Scoping the claude side to `hooks/bin/` instead left
# `plugins-claude/git-span/hooks/hooks.json` exposed — one generated file, on one
# of the two shipped plugins, reachable by any build that touches hook
# registration. `hooks.json` is not a classifiable basename, so the classifier
# refuses it on the gate and nothing downstream catches it.
#
# To be precise about the shape, since the obvious reading is wrong: a changeset
# containing *only* that file is silent regardless, because the uncovered-writes
# check short-circuits below two paths — a coupling needs two files to exist. The
# exposure was any commit pairing the regenerated `hooks.json` with at least one
# real edit, where it appears as a spurious extra entry beside a genuine one.
# That is worse than it sounds: a short list mixing one actionable path with one
# unactionable one is harder to dismiss correctly than a list that is uniformly
# noise.
plugins-claude/git-span/hooks/
plugins-codex/git-span/hooks/
